{
  "module": "Output side: from scores to text",
  "lesson": {
    "slug": "next-token-sampling",
    "title": "The next-token distribution and choosing a token",
    "summary": "What one pass of the model produces (a probability for each possible next token, at every position) and how a token is then chosen from it by sampling.",
    "covers": ["next-token-distribution", "sampling"],
    "prerequisites": [
      {
        "lesson": "logits-softmax",
        "reason": "The distribution is the softmax of the logits, so both must already be understood."
      }
    ]
  },
  "screens": [
    {
      "ref": "one-pass",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Put a piece of text through the model once, a single "
            },
            {
              "text": "forward pass",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": ". What comes out?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Not a token, and not a reply. At each position in the text the network produces a set of logits, and softmax turns each set into probabilities."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "So the output of one pass is a "
            },
            {
              "text": "probability for every token in the vocabulary",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": ", saying how likely it is to come next."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 19)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "every-position",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "It does this at "
            },
            {
              "text": "every position",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " in the text at once, not only at the end."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Take the text "
            },
            {
              "text": "The cat sat",
              "italic": true
            },
            {
              "text": ". The result is three distributions:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "text": "at "
              },
              {
                "text": "The",
                "italic": true
              },
              {
                "text": ": how likely each token is to follow "
              },
              {
                "text": "The",
                "italic": true
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "text": "at "
              },
              {
                "text": "cat",
                "italic": true
              },
              {
                "text": ": how likely each token is to follow "
              },
              {
                "text": "The cat",
                "italic": true
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "text": "at "
              },
              {
                "text": "sat",
                "italic": true
              },
              {
                "text": ": how likely each token is to follow "
              },
              {
                "text": "The cat sat",
                "italic": true
              }
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Each one is conditioned on the tokens up to and including that position, and nothing after it. When you want the model to continue a text, it is the last one that matters."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 19, 68)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "toy-distribution",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "A toy example. After the text "
            },
            {
              "text": "The cat sat on the",
              "italic": true
            },
            {
              "text": ", a model might give these probabilities to four candidate tokens. The numbers are invented for illustration:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "text": "mat: 0.657"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "text": "sofa: 0.242"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "text": "floor: 0.089"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "text": "moon: 0.012"
              }
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "This is everything the network itself gives you. It has not picked "
            },
            {
              "text": "mat",
              "italic": true
            },
            {
              "text": ", or any other token. It has only said how likely each one is."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 19)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "sampling",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Choosing an actual token from that distribution is a "
            },
            {
              "text": "separate step",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": ", called "
            },
            {
              "text": "sampling",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": ". It happens outside the network."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "The network computes the distribution. Sampling is the rule you apply to it to get one token."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "tone": "note",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Softmax and sampling are different jobs. Softmax turns scores into probabilities. Sampling turns probabilities into one chosen token."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 15, 19)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "greedy",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "The simplest rule is "
            },
            {
              "text": "greedy",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": ": always take the most probable token."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "With the toy distribution, greedy always picks "
            },
            {
              "text": "mat",
              "italic": true
            },
            {
              "text": ". Given the same distribution, it always picks the same token."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "That is predictable, but it means the text can never take an unlikely turn."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 15)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "random-draw",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "The other basic rule is to "
            },
            {
              "text": "draw at random in proportion to the probabilities",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": ", like rolling a weighted die."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "With the toy distribution, "
            },
            {
              "text": "mat",
              "italic": true
            },
            {
              "text": " is drawn about two times in three (66%), "
            },
            {
              "text": "sofa",
              "italic": true
            },
            {
              "text": " about one time in four (24%), "
            },
            {
              "text": "floor",
              "italic": true
            },
            {
              "text": " about one time in eleven, and "
            },
            {
              "text": "moon",
              "italic": true
            },
            {
              "text": " about one time in eighty."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Now the same text can be continued in different ways from one run to the next, and unlikely tokens do sometimes appear."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 15)"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
